# One line ending for everyone, whatever core.autocrlf says on the machine that checks it out:
# the sha256 pinned in skills/vendor/LOCK is of LF bytes, and a CRLF checkout (Windows) would break it.
* text=auto eol=lf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.ttf binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.gif binary
